    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` feature on `POST /api/owners` (and it's returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`), keeping each piece of logic in its natural home:\n\n**New logic in one focused unit**\n- `AgeBand` helper (`rest/function/owner/AgeBand.java`) \u2014 a pure lookup, mirroring the existing `Locality`/`Postcode` style: given a birth date and registration date it returns `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364) or `SENIOR` (65+), or `null` when either date is absent. Age is measured with `Period.between(...)` **against the registration date**, per the spec.\n\n**Wiring \u2014 reused existing patterns rather than adding a new pipeline step**\n- `Owner` model: added the persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter, alongside `registrationDate`.\n- `OwnerMapper`: `birthDate` maps automatically by name (request \u2192 entity \u2192 response); `ageBand` is a derived read-only field computed via `AgeBand.of(...)` \u2014 consistent with how `membershipNumber`, `locality`, and `contactPreference` are already derived in the mapper, so no persisted column and no extra function step were needed.\n- `openapi.yml`: `birthDate` added to `OwnerFields` (read/write) and `ageBand` to `Owner` (read-only) so the generated DTOs carry both.\n- DB schema: `birth_date DATE` added to all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) so the persisted value survives to the `GET` read.\n\n**Verification** \u2014 `./mvnw -o test`: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS. The acceptance test creates an owner with `birthDate=1990-01-01` and reads back `ageBand=ADULT`.",
